{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they sent him.</b> An expression of escorting with honor, likewise \"and Abraham went with them to send them off\" (Genesis 18:16)." "And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that the meaning of \"and he charged concerning him\" is — because עַל refers to others — the charge that he warned and commanded to proclaim, that no man touch him or his wife:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:24.584733573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}